==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|house warming}}
* {{l|en|house-warming}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|house|warming}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-housewarming.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} A [[party]] to celebrate moving into a new [[home]].
#: {{syn|en|house-heating|q1=archaic}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=5|passage=In the eyes of Mr. Farquhar Fenelon Cooke the apotheosis of the Celebrity was complete. The people of Asquith were not only willing to attend the '''house-warming''', but had been worked up to the pitch of eagerness.}}
# The act of [[welcoming]] a person/family to their [[new]]ly purchased or newly rented [[home]].
#: ''a '''housewarming''' gift''
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2004|volume=89|issue=4|page=580|title=Gadney's Immunity|author=Jacob M Appel|journal=Southwest Review|passage=They had their first argument on the evening Gadney moved in, their '''housewarming''' spat, he later called it.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|title=The Offering|author=John Kinsella|passage=Fortunately, Dave had left them a packet of rollie tobacco and papers for a '''housewarming'''}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|house cooling party}}

